WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.980
Millions of learners today
are watching videos online

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.650
using platforms such as
Khan Academy, Coursera, edX,

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:10.990
and YouTube.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.870
As thousands of learners
interact with the same video

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.100
content, their
watching behaviors

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.900
lead to collective
interaction patterns.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.220
These patterns might indicate to
points of confusion, interest,

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.140
and importance.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.110
We introduced LectureScape,
a video player

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.000
that's powered by a set of
data-driven video interaction

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.590
techniques.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.340
LectureScape enhances
the video timeline

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.580
to help learners identify and
navigate to important parts

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:38.700
of the video.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.230
Unlike a traditional
linear timeline,

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:45.590
the rollercoaster timeline is 2D
with an embodied visualization

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.930
of second-by-second
navigation frequency

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:51.650
of all learners and
resulting interaction peaks.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.980
It also modifies the
timeline dragging behavior

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:58.070
by creating a sense of
friction while dragging

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:00.350
the playhead around the keys.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:04.250
As a result, frames near
the peaks are exposed longer

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:07.190
and are easier to
precisely navigate to.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.980
In addition to collective
watching traces,

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:13.520
LecureScape also keeps track
of personal watching traces

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.905
and visualizes in
real time the segments

00:01:15.905 --> 00:01:19.740
of the video that the
current learner has watched.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:23.460
Clicking on the generated
segment replays that segment.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.890
LectureScape uses
interaction data

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.760
to better support searching
for relevant information

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:30.660
inside a video.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.990
When the learner types
in a search word,

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.090
the search timeline
appears below the video.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:39.090
It visualizes the positions
of certain results

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:42.190
as well as the relative
importance of each.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:44.550
Our search algorithm
rewords results

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:48.170
in sections of the video
where more learners watched.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.820
LectureScape uses
interaction data

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.360
to create a visual
summarization of a videoclip.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.170
LectureScape presents a
strip of visual highlights

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:00.300
below the video to
enable a quick overview

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.070
of the important points.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:05.700
These are the frames frequently
watched by other learners.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.250
Clicking on a frame plays
that point in the video.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:12.400
The learner can also bookmark
their own frame of interest

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.330
and add notes, which is then
added to the highlight stream

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.798
below the video.

00:02:18.798 --> 00:02:21.760
In educational videos,
instructors often

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.790
refer to concepts and
formulas introduced earlier

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:27.130
in the video, but
the referred slides

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.870
are no longer
available on screen.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.740
LectureScape automatically
pins a relevant frame

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:36.000
next to that video
for a quick reference.

